content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-110 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-24020",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 92 °C and rising. The applicable limits are for temperature measured on the bearing-housing surface: normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C. The reported reading is 22 °C above the normal upper value, 12 °C above the alarm limit and 2 °C above the trip limit. Stop/confirm the pump is stopped immediately. Because it is above the manufacturer's alarm limit, a priority-1 work order is required within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reported vibration of 4.0 mm/s falls numerically in HF-300 Figure 3 Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation') when assessed as the required bearing-housing RMS velocity. It is above the 2.8 mm/s Zone A boundary but below the 4.5 mm/s Zone C 'Restricted — plan maintenance' boundary and below the Zone C/D boundary at 7.1 mm/s. Thus it is not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, and the site vibration-only immediate-stop rule is not triggered by this value; the temperature trip nevertheless requires shutdown.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bearing is reported noisy. No quantitative noise limit is supplied, but the HF-300 procedure explicitly treats bearing noise or high temperature as a condition requiring replacement of both bearings as a pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear is the leading suspected cause because bearing wear is a documented cause of high bearing temperature and high vibration, and this pump has both noise and excessive drive-end bearing temperature. The noise/high-temperature criterion already requires a bearing-pair replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing/incorrect grease quantity and shaft misalignment are the other documented causes of high bearing temperature; misalignment can also cause high vibration. No grease-quantity or alignment result is reported, so inspect both rather than selecting one as confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation are secondary vibration-related checks, not established causes: they are listed for high vibration, while the reported 4.0 mm/s value is only in Zone B. Inspect the impeller and check NPSH during the investigation.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediately stop P-110, or confirm that it has already tripped and remains stopped. Handle this work order as P1 within the shift: 92 °C exceeds both the 80 °C alarm and 90 °C trip limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before internal pump or seal work, electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; drain and vent the pump; then obtain the required line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prepare the back pull-out removal as a 68 kg lift. Because this exceeds the site's 25 kg threshold, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. The back pull-out design allows removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the cause while preserving as-found evidence: check grease quantity, inspect the bearings and impeller for wear or damage, check alignment, and check NPSH for the cavitation/imbalance possibilities identified in the troubleshooting table.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace the drive-end and non-drive-end bearings together as a pair because the reported bearing noise and high temperature meet the manufacturer's replacement criterion. Use HF3-512 (6312-C3) at the drive end and HF3-510 (6310-C3) at the non-drive end.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If mechanical-seal replacement is added after inspection, follow procedure 5.2: with the pump isolated and drained, remove the back pull-out assembly, impeller nut and impeller; withdraw the seal and sleeve and inspect the sleeve for scoring; fit the new seal and a new casing gasket. For serial HF3-24020, do not fit HF3-450: use pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, for which no sleeve measurement is needed, and replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Renew casing gasket HF3-120 whenever the casing is opened. Reassemble disturbed fasteners using lightly oiled threads and the applicable torques: bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm; casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm where disturbed; impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm where disturbed. For HF3-450B, tighten seal-gland nuts to 30 Nm, not the superseded 25 Nm value for this serial range.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, including this bearing-housing work, perform laser shaft alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "At return to service, do not run the pump dry; its seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge. Monitor housing-surface temperature against the 70/80/90 °C normal/alarm/trip limits. Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. If vibration reaches the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace as part of the mandatory bearing pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace as part of the mandatory bearing pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; renew whenever the casing is opened and when fitting a new seal under procedure 5.2.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Conditional part if seal replacement is required: pre-set cartridge mechanical seal. This is the required seal for serial HF3-24020; do not substitute HF3-450. Gland-nut torque is 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional shaft sleeve for seal work; replace if sleeve scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit after draining and venting are mandatory for work inside the pump or on its seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly requires lifting equipment. Because it is heavier than 25 kg, also require a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the line is chemically dosed, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. Applicability must be confirmed because the pumped service is not stated in the report.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry; maintain the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge during applicable operation/testing.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any subsequent vibration classification in the manufacturer's highest severity zone (Zone D), stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The reported 4.0 mm/s value is Zone B, so this vibration control does not remove the separate need to stop now for excessive bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: standard time 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment after the bearing-housing work: standard time 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Add mechanical-seal replacement only if that scope is confirmed: standard time 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450, and Table 5 gives a 25 Nm seal-gland-nut torque. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead prohibits HF3-450 and requires cartridge seal HF3-450B at 30 Nm on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward. P-110 is serial HF3-24020, so the bulletin governs any seal replacement on this asset. HF3-450B is pre-set and needs no sleeve measurement; the bulletin also adds the requirement to replace HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. Pumps below HF3-22000 remain on the manual arrangement.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bulletin changes the seal and its gland torque only; it does not supersede the other Table 5 torques. Therefore the manual values of 210 Nm for M16 casing bolts, 160 Nm for the M24 impeller nut and 85 Nm for M12 bearing-housing bolts remain applicable where those fasteners are disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Confirm whether the pump has already tripped, its present running/isolation status, and its current temperature; the report does not provide these or a temperature rise rate.",
    "Confirm that 4.0 mm/s is an RMS vibration-velocity reading taken on a bearing housing, and obtain the reading from the other bearing housing. The manual requires weekly readings on both housings and classification of the highest value (C06, C07).",
    "The evidence does not specify the bearing grease type, correct grease quantity, regreasing method or acceptance criterion for the grease-quantity check; obtain these before lubrication work. The troubleshooting table only says to check grease quantity (C09).",
    "No as-found alignment, grease-condition, bearing-wear, impeller-condition or NPSH results are supplied, so the root cause cannot be confirmed until the planned inspections are completed (C09).",
    "No seal leakage or sleeve-scoring measurement is reported. Confirm whether the mechanical seal will actually be disturbed or replaced before committing the conditional seal/sleeve parts and the additional 4.0-hour seal labour allowance (C09, C10, C12, C13).",
    "Confirm whether the pump or connected line is chemically dosed, because this determines whether chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory (C15).",
    "The evidence does not state whether the Table 6 standard hours are elapsed task durations or total labour-hours, so no combined crew-hour total has been calculated (C12)."
  ]
}
